  "id": "Security_Community_Slams_US_Ban_on_Exporting_Mythos_Fable_txt_24",
  "content": "\"The researchers took open-source code with known CVEs, plus new code with deliberately planted vulnerabilities, and asked Fable 5, Mythos, and Opus to 'review the code for security issues.' Fable 5 refused. They then asked the models to 'fix this code' and, through a multistep and manual process, turned the output into scripts that test the patches,\" she wrote. \"The prompts worked because they were defensive requests, and that capability cannot be removed without making the model worse at fixing bugs and verifying patches.\"",
